{"school":{"dbn":"20K104","name":"P.S./I.S. 104 The Fort Hamilton School","boro":"Brooklyn","district":"20","district_label":"District 20","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"K-8","grades":"K to 8","status":"open","enrollment":1023,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"9115 5 AVENUE, Brooklyn, NY 11209","phone":"718-236-9003","website":"www.psis104.com","directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/middle-school/67487","accessibility":"Partially Accessible","overview":"We emphasize developing the whole child. As a school centered on Civic Leadership and responsibility, we provide opportunities for students to give back to their school in the form of service squads and to the community through participation in a variety of altruistic endeavors.   We offer many opportunities aligned with skills and talents that lead to college and career readiness including: Student Government and Leadership, College visits, AAA Safety Patrol, The Junior Achievement Program/Business Finance Park, Virtual Enterprise, Participation in theater, visual arts, vocal music, sports during and after-school, Annual STEAM Expo, National History Day Fair, Respect For All activities, Mouse Squad to assist in maintaining technology in the school, Musicale Performances and Art Exhibits. We have maintained a level of commitment toward school-wide technology to continue to prepare our students for college and career readiness. Available technology includes: Smart Boards in all classrooms, Desktops, Portable Laptop Carts, a Computer Lab, iPads for every student, and 3D printers. We offer Accelerated classes in Algebra, Living Environment and Spanish leading to High School credit.  We also offer a variety of clubs and electives for our students.","start_time":"08:10am","end_time":"02:29pm","languages":null,"subway":"R to 95th St","bus":"B1, B16, B37, B63, B70, B8, S53, S79-SBS, S93, X27, X28, X37, X38","shared_building":"0","neighborhood":"Fort Hamilton","latitude":40.6182,"